SplashBitmap kept its colour data when the alpha channel it was asked for
could not be allocated. Callers only check getDataPtr() (Splash::scaleImage
and others) and then write the alpha channel through the null alpha pointer:
heap corruption in the wasm guest (dlfree trap), a crash natively. Treat a
failed alpha allocation like a failed data allocation.

